WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:22.720
The second day of the Satipatthana course is over.

00:22.720 --> 00:40.120
This evening let us go through this discourse and understand in relation to the actual practice

00:40.120 --> 00:53.800
that we are doing.

00:53.800 --> 01:05.840
The name of the discourse is Mahasatipatthana Sutthana, Sutthana means discourse.

01:05.840 --> 01:16.460
It is said Mahasatipatthana, the word maha means great, big.

01:16.460 --> 01:24.160
That means there is something smaller than this and yes there is another discourse given

01:24.160 --> 01:31.560
by Buddha on Satipatthana which is smaller than this discourse.

01:31.560 --> 01:42.320
This discourse is maha, bigger because it gives, it deals with some more subjects in

01:42.320 --> 01:49.120
detail therefore it is called Mahasatipatthana.

01:49.120 --> 02:03.520
Sati is awareness, a very important faculty of dhamma as we discussed yesterday.

02:03.520 --> 02:14.480
Sati is one of our indriyas, a faculty which one has to master to develop in dhamma.

02:14.520 --> 02:25.840
Sati is one of the bala, the forces, the strength which one must develop to master dhamma.

02:25.840 --> 02:35.160
Sati is one of the factors of enlightenment which one has to develop to get fully enlightened.

02:35.160 --> 02:43.160
Sati is also one of the eight full noble paths, samma, sati.

02:43.160 --> 02:52.760
Sati plays a very important role in the practice of dhamma.

02:52.760 --> 03:02.160
The literal meaning of the word sati is and very commonly used nowadays in other languages

03:02.160 --> 03:14.600
of India, present languages of India as smriti which means memory, remembrance.

03:14.600 --> 03:23.520
But when you practice vipashyana there is no memory involved, you are not remembering

03:23.520 --> 03:27.440
something of the past.

03:27.440 --> 03:36.160
Here what you have to remember is, remember your object of meditation.

03:36.160 --> 03:41.280
That means the reality within the framework of the body, the reality pertaining to mind

03:41.280 --> 03:42.280
and matter.

03:42.280 --> 03:47.880
You should always remember that your mind does not wander away from this reality.

03:47.880 --> 03:51.400
That is in that sense you can say remembrance.

03:51.400 --> 03:57.560
But in a better way of understanding let us say sati means awareness and this is what

03:57.560 --> 03:58.560
it is.

03:58.560 --> 04:00.400
You are aware.

04:00.400 --> 04:04.840
You can't be aware of the past, you can't be aware of the future.

04:04.840 --> 04:07.520
You can be aware of the present.

04:07.520 --> 04:14.720
The reality of this moment as it is, this is sati, pathana.

04:14.720 --> 04:17.260
One gets established.

04:17.260 --> 04:26.640
The word pa says extensively, you get established extensively.

04:26.640 --> 04:28.260
What extensively?

04:28.260 --> 04:35.600
That means it is not mere awareness, along with that awareness there is element of panya,

04:35.600 --> 04:37.480
element of wisdom.

04:37.480 --> 04:44.160
You are not merely aware of the truth pertaining to mind and matter, you are also aware of

04:44.160 --> 04:49.960
the nature of this truth pertaining to mind and matter, how it keeps on arising, passing

04:49.960 --> 04:57.120
away, arising, passing away, how it is a source of misery, how it is no I, no mind, how it

04:57.120 --> 04:58.120
is substance-less.

04:58.120 --> 05:10.320
All that has not to be understood merely at the intellectual level with direct experience.

05:10.320 --> 05:17.440
And therefore pathana, panya, the bhavanamaya panya is there, with your own direct experience

05:17.440 --> 05:23.360
you develop your awareness with the wisdom which makes you understand the reality in

05:23.360 --> 05:30.240
its true nature, not just as it appears to be, not just as it seems to be, but in its

05:30.240 --> 05:39.240
true nature and that is why it is maha sati pathana sutta.

05:39.240 --> 05:53.480
When the discourse starts, evam me sutam, this is what was heard by me, this was heard

05:53.480 --> 05:56.360
by me.

05:56.360 --> 06:08.560
These are not the words of buddha, somebody else says, this was heard by me.

06:08.560 --> 06:16.920
These are the words of someone else, there is a history behind it and a very important

06:16.920 --> 06:24.680
history which a vipassana meditator should know.

06:24.680 --> 06:36.080
At the ripened age of 80 years when buddha passed away, most of his students who were

06:36.080 --> 06:44.360
present at that time and who had reached the final goal of arhanthood, fully liberated,

06:44.360 --> 06:51.560
they understood the law of nature, everyone who takes birth has to pass away.

06:51.560 --> 06:56.800
Whether one is buddha or an ordinary person makes no difference.

06:56.800 --> 07:02.260
When time ripens, one has to pass away.

07:02.260 --> 07:11.980
For those who were not developed in dhamma, they felt very sorry, very sad, some of them

07:11.980 --> 07:18.100
even started crying.

07:18.100 --> 07:29.540
There was one person who felt very happy.

07:29.540 --> 07:39.500
An old monk, in age old, not in wisdom, he felt very happy, oh good, this old man has

07:39.500 --> 07:43.300
passed away.

07:43.300 --> 07:48.860
All the time we were under his clutches, do this, don't do this, do this, don't do this,

07:48.860 --> 07:52.420
now we are free to do whatever we like.

07:52.420 --> 07:57.980
One of his teachings, attahi attanonathu, you are your own master, now I can be my own

07:57.980 --> 08:01.780
master, wonderful.

08:01.780 --> 08:12.940
That shows that such elements had entered in the sangha who were not interested in dhamma.

08:12.940 --> 08:22.100
They just took robes because they found by entering the sangha, becoming a monk in the

08:22.100 --> 08:28.000
name of buddha, will give them some status in the society.

08:28.000 --> 08:32.620
They can live a comfortable life, people will give more arms to them than they would have

08:32.620 --> 08:42.300
received otherwise, and they will get more respect, they were not interested in dhamma.

08:42.300 --> 08:55.680
Now this person, I feel extremely grateful to this person, thankful to this person, why?

08:55.680 --> 09:02.860
Because when he announced that wonderful buddha has passed away, one of the chief disciples

09:02.860 --> 09:13.420
of buddha, when he heard this, he thought even today if there are such people, what

09:13.420 --> 09:23.700
is going to happen in the future, later on such elements will become predominant, and

09:23.700 --> 09:30.940
they will just distort the teaching of buddha in their own way, and actually this happened

09:30.940 --> 09:35.120
also after some time.

09:35.120 --> 09:37.880
How to save it?

09:37.880 --> 09:47.580
The words of buddha, the teachings of buddha, he became enlightened at the age of 35, and

09:47.580 --> 10:00.920
he passed away at the age of 80, for 45 years, day and night, hardly two or three hours he

10:00.920 --> 10:10.860
will lie down for sleep, which is not sleep, awareness and equanimity, awareness and wisdom,

10:10.860 --> 10:20.460
to give rest to the body, rest of the time he was just teaching dhamma.

10:20.460 --> 10:27.460
He taught, he gave 82,000 sermons.

10:27.460 --> 10:34.360
Over 2,000 sermons were given by leading disciples of buddha, who were urhans.

10:34.360 --> 10:39.280
So in all 84,000 sermons.

10:39.280 --> 10:54.400
Now this elderly disciple, by the name of Mahakassapa, he decides that all the teaching

10:54.400 --> 11:06.220
of buddha must be compiled together, and we should try to preserve it for the coming

11:06.220 --> 11:14.640
generations, so that people do not change it.

11:14.640 --> 11:23.320
Quite possible later on, persons like this fellow will put their own words in the mouth

11:23.320 --> 11:31.960
of buddha and they will say, buddha said so, they will take freedom from certain disciplines

11:31.960 --> 11:36.800
which are very essential for the progress of dhamma, and they will say, buddha gave

11:36.800 --> 11:45.600
this permission, and things like that, which after a few centuries it did happen.

11:45.600 --> 11:55.080
We must preserve the actual words of buddha, while there are people who are direct disciples

11:55.080 --> 12:01.960
of buddha, who are eyewitness to buddha's teaching, who heard buddha's teaching.

12:01.960 --> 12:12.960
So he decided to call a meeting of 500 urhans, fully liberated persons, elderly persons,

12:12.960 --> 12:27.280
elderly monks, let us sit together and recite all the teachings of buddha, compile them,

12:27.280 --> 12:33.800
and announce it as authenticated.

12:33.800 --> 12:38.920
This is just immediately after the death of buddha.

12:38.920 --> 12:46.840
If this is compiled after 100 years or 200 years, people may accept, may not accept,

12:46.840 --> 12:50.560
it should be done now.

12:50.560 --> 13:00.680
So this Mahakasapa, a very wise person, he made this decision, he gathered 500 elderly

13:00.680 --> 13:08.880
urhans, well even a few handful could do that, but just to impress the people of that time

13:09.280 --> 13:17.840
and people of future, 500 of them joined together, and they read out every word, they recited

13:17.840 --> 13:27.840
every word of buddha, and then gave it a seal of authenticity.

13:27.840 --> 13:38.880
When he selected 500, somebody said no, this congregation, this gathering will not be

13:38.880 --> 13:46.680
a perfect gathering unless we have ananda as one of the members.

13:46.680 --> 13:53.560
So have only 499, let ananda be a member to make it 500.

13:53.560 --> 13:57.800
Now who is this ananda?

13:57.800 --> 14:05.120
Buddha was cousin brother of buddha, Gautama the buddha, was born on the same day as Gautama

14:05.120 --> 14:08.560
the buddha was born.

14:08.560 --> 14:16.200
He was with him in the childhood, he was with him during the youth, and when buddha renounced

14:16.200 --> 14:23.000
the householder's life, went out and became enlightened, then he was one amongst many

14:23.040 --> 14:30.320
family members who also renounced their householder's life and joined him, and since then he was

14:30.320 --> 14:34.640
with him all the time.

14:34.640 --> 14:45.040
When buddha started teaching, the number of followers started spreading, the work started

14:45.080 --> 14:53.440
spreading, naturally he wanted some assistant, a number of assistants came near him to help

14:53.440 --> 15:06.440
him, to serve him, but quite a few of them came with some motives, the motive was, here

15:06.440 --> 15:18.600
he is a fully enlightened person, he is against these miracles, he has the power of miracles,

15:18.600 --> 15:26.160
no doubt, but he doesn't want his followers to show miracles.

15:26.160 --> 15:33.040
If I am very close to him, I will be fortunate to see some of the miracles being performed

15:33.040 --> 15:40.040
by him, such motive was there with some of these attendants, personal attendants.

15:40.040 --> 15:49.040
Buddha had refused to answer certain questions, philosophical questions, he said they are

15:49.040 --> 15:54.720
useless, meaningless, don't waste your time on them.

15:54.720 --> 15:59.520
Now some attendants thought that he doesn't want to say anything on this subject in public,

15:59.520 --> 16:05.840
but perhaps if I am very close, then he may explain, I better be very close, I better

16:05.840 --> 16:08.560
serve.

16:08.560 --> 16:17.740
Such people could not stay with him longer, sooner or later they have to leave.

16:17.740 --> 16:31.500
People keep on changing and as he grew in age, he became 55 years old, getting old,

16:31.500 --> 16:37.180
so people thought that there must be a stable personal assistant with him, he also accepted

16:37.180 --> 16:44.820
yes some responsible stable personal assistant, a private secretary is necessary.

16:44.900 --> 16:54.900
Many of the elderly monks were very eager to take that post, to serve him so closely,

16:54.900 --> 17:03.480
but Buddha had a liking towards Ananda, and Ananda is mum, he doesn't say a word, people

17:03.480 --> 17:11.980
know that if Ananda says yes, Buddha will accept him, Ananda does not say yes, when

17:12.140 --> 17:21.140
they persuaded him he said I have got my terms, if Buddha accepts my terms, then I will be

17:21.140 --> 17:27.980
his personal assistant, somebody putting terms before Buddha to be a personal assistant,

17:27.980 --> 17:28.980
what are your terms?

17:28.980 --> 17:36.300
He put up some seven or eight terms, and out of that one was very healthy terms, very wholesome

17:36.300 --> 17:38.340
terms.

17:38.340 --> 17:47.020
One of that was that whenever you give any discourse anywhere, if I am present, perfectly

17:47.020 --> 17:53.940
alright, if by any reason I am not present and you give a discourse, then when you come

17:53.940 --> 17:59.660
back you must repeat that discourse to me.

17:59.660 --> 18:05.980
Buddha accepted all his conditions, including this, so from the age of 55 to the age of

18:06.620 --> 18:15.620
80, 25 years, every discourse that Buddha gave was heard by this person, Ananda, even

18:15.620 --> 18:21.980
the discourses before that also were heard by him, but these 25 years he was like a shadow

18:21.980 --> 18:30.420
with Buddha, every discourse was heard by him, and here was a wonderful person, he had

18:30.500 --> 18:36.980
such a wonderful faculty, from some of his good parmes of the past, and also due to

18:36.980 --> 18:45.980
his practice of this life, he had developed the faculty of memory, he hears something

18:45.980 --> 18:55.940
once, enough, it is like tape recorded, what you are doing here, it is like computerized,

18:55.940 --> 19:03.860
anytime you ask anything, he will just repeat word to word, this was his wonderful faculty.

19:03.860 --> 19:11.740
So people said if Ananda is not there, something is missing, he should be there, but he can't

19:11.740 --> 19:20.740
be there, because this is a gathering of Arhans, and he is not an Arhan.

19:20.740 --> 19:31.620
Understand Ananda served Buddha for 25 years, so close to him, Ananda was his cousin brother,

19:31.620 --> 19:42.700
so close to him, Ananda was his great devotee, so close to him, and yet he could not become

19:42.700 --> 19:49.700
Arhan, he was only Sotapanna, the first stage of liberation, when one experiences the liberation

19:51.060 --> 19:58.060
stage, the stage beyond mind and matter for the first time, very important stage, but

19:58.060 --> 20:05.060
still it is the first stage of liberation, after that you have got higher stage, you

20:05.060 --> 20:11.580
have got higher stage than that, and then you have the highest stage of Arhan, and here

20:11.700 --> 20:22.700
he is having reached only the first stage, this again for us to understand that Buddha

20:22.700 --> 20:33.700
cannot liberate anybody, each individual has to work out one's own salvation, he had no

20:33.700 --> 20:40.700
time, he was just serving Buddha all the time, he could not progress, although he knew

20:41.660 --> 20:52.660
Dhamma perfectly well, not one, not two, thousands of persons whom he taught became Arhans, and

20:52.860 --> 21:01.860
he himself was not Arhan, and in this gathering, how can a known Arhan be there, so Mahakasrapa

21:01.860 --> 21:08.860
goes to him and tells him, well look, well look, Vandivalananda, you were very busy

21:09.900 --> 21:16.900
serving Buddha, now Buddha is no more, you know the technique so well, because your own

21:17.660 --> 21:24.660
disciples have reached the stage of Arhanthood, now you have got so much time, why not work,

21:25.500 --> 21:31.540
become Arhan, so that you can come in our gathering, join our gathering, this is the

21:31.540 --> 21:37.700
aim that we have of this gathering, and you will be very great asset to it, Ananda was

21:37.700 --> 21:44.700
very glad, wonderful, yes, I didn't have much time before, now I have got time, nothing

21:44.700 --> 21:51.700
else, all time is there at my disposal, wait for few days, I will practice, I will become

21:51.900 --> 21:58.900
Arhanth and join you, and he started working, started working very vigorously, I must become

22:02.940 --> 22:09.940
an Arhanth, I must become an Arhanth, when he was teaching others, he used to say, don't

22:09.940 --> 22:16.940
develop ego, this ego is dangerous for you, it will be an obstacle, and when he practices

22:24.380 --> 22:31.380
himself, this ego becomes important, I must become Arhanth, I must become Arhanth, many

22:32.100 --> 22:38.180
a time the teacher forgets what he teaches others, when he practices himself, he forgets

22:38.220 --> 22:45.220
his own teaching and this is what happened, he didn't move an inch, now tomorrow they

22:47.020 --> 22:54.020
have to start this conference, and Mahakasrappa comes to Ananda and tells him, look we have

22:54.980 --> 23:01.980
waited so long, we can't be waiting, there are 499 persons waiting for the conference

23:02.460 --> 23:09.460
to start by tomorrow morning, you are Arhanth or no Arhanth, if you are no Arhanth, I take

23:09.740 --> 23:15.420
somebody else, I will start my work, if you are Arhanth, you are welcome, yes, yes, yes,

23:15.420 --> 23:22.420
one night more, I will try this one night more, and again try, try, I must become Arhanth,

23:25.180 --> 23:30.980
this is the only night for me, I must become Arhanth, the first part of the night, the

23:31.180 --> 23:38.180
middle part of the night, the last part of the night, light passes away, the sun is rising,

23:39.860 --> 23:46.860
he is so exhausted, he doesn't cry, at least this good quality, he is not successful, and

23:48.060 --> 23:51.820
that much he knows that one should not cry when one is not successful, he accept the

23:51.820 --> 23:58.820
fact, well I accept the fact, I am not an Arhanth, now let me take rest, let me take

24:00.980 --> 24:07.980
rest, I am not an Arhanth, I am just a Sotapanna, a Sotapanna, he was with the reality of this

24:13.180 --> 24:20.180
moment as it is, when he was aiming for something to become Arhanth, his mind was always in

24:20.660 --> 24:27.660
the future, not in the present, and now I am not an Arhanth, he accept this reality,

24:27.940 --> 24:34.940
I am just a Sotapanna, I am taking rest, I am taking rest, and observing the sensations

24:36.940 --> 24:43.940
inside, arising, passing, arising, passing, this is the way of taking rest, for good meditators,

24:44.220 --> 24:51.220
I am taking rest, and before his head could reach the pillow, he was an Arhanth, when

24:52.220 --> 24:59.220
you, how much effort, if you make over-exertion, then you lose the balance of your mind, middle

25:01.820 --> 25:08.820
path, neither there must be one extreme of laxity that you don't do anything, nor your

25:09.260 --> 25:16.260
effort must be so extreme that you lose the balance of your mind, and Ananda becomes Arhanth,

25:16.540 --> 25:23.540
and Ananda becomes Arhanth, and he joins the conference. Now questions are asked to Ananda,

25:27.620 --> 25:34.620
what did Buddha say? All the teachings of Buddha were compiled, and three divisions

25:35.780 --> 25:42.780
were made, that is why they are called Ti Pitika, Ti means three, Pitika means baskets,

25:43.260 --> 25:50.260
baskets in those days, the books were kept in baskets, there is three groups of the teaching

25:50.700 --> 25:57.700
of Buddha, the one is Sutta Pitaka, where is long or short discourses to the public

26:02.540 --> 26:09.540
were accumulated, compiled, then Vinaya Pitaka, his discourses specially to the monks, the

26:09.540 --> 26:16.540
nuns, about their discipline, about their Seela, for householders five Seela, good enough,

26:18.580 --> 26:25.580
but for a monk, for a nun, over 200 Seelas, and this is what this old man resented, oh

26:27.580 --> 26:34.580
so much restriction on us, all those instructions to the monks, to the nuns, they were given

26:39.660 --> 26:46.660
by the monks, they were compiled in Vinaya Pitaka, and then the third called Abhidhamma,

26:46.820 --> 26:53.820
higher Dhamma, Dhamma, law of nature, the truth, deeper truth, which it is not easy

26:57.100 --> 27:04.100
to understand by ordinary person, one has to meditate very deeply to understand it,

27:04.540 --> 27:11.860
this is an analytical study of the entire mind-matter phenomenon, the entire field,

27:11.860 --> 27:18.860
in such detail it is explained in Abhidhamma, starting from the apparent truth to the ultimate

27:21.300 --> 27:28.300
truth, all the details of the reality pertaining to the matter, all the details of the reality

27:34.220 --> 27:40.180
pertaining to the mind, all the details pertaining to the reality, reality pertaining to the

27:40.180 --> 27:47.180
mental factors, the mental concomitants, the mental contents, the matter in the language

27:48.900 --> 27:55.900
of those days was called Rupa, the mind was called Chitta, and the mental contents, Chetashika,

27:55.900 --> 28:02.900
fully explained how they interact, how one starts influencing the other, how the matter

28:11.260 --> 28:18.260
stimulates the arising of the mind, how the mind stimulates the arising of the matter,

28:19.620 --> 28:23.500
how the mind stimulates the arising of the mind, how the matter stimulates the arising

28:23.500 --> 28:30.500
of the matter, all these interconnections and the currents and cross currents going

28:31.580 --> 28:38.580
on deep inside are fully explained, they cannot be understood just by reading Abhidhamma,

28:39.420 --> 28:44.860
only by the practice of Vipashyana, at a very deep stage such things become clear, that

28:44.860 --> 28:51.860
is the third Pethaka, Abhidhamma Pethaka, all these three, so far as Sutta Pethaka,

28:53.700 --> 29:00.700
and Abhidhamma Pethaka were concerned, Ananda was asked questions about that, so far as

29:00.700 --> 29:07.700
Vinaya Pethaka was concerned, another Arhant by the name of Upali, he was perfect in the

29:07.700 --> 29:14.700
discipline of monks and nuns, he was asked questions, now this comes in the Sutta Pethaka,

29:15.620 --> 29:22.620
and Ananda says, this is what I heard, Evam Me Sutam, in many of these Suttas, we find

29:28.900 --> 29:35.900
the Sutta start with these words, Evam Me Sutam, this is what I heard, he heard directly

29:36.500 --> 29:43.500
from the Mahavata Buddha, this is what I heard, and then he is good enough to give a description

29:54.540 --> 30:01.540
of the situation, the situation in which this discourse was given, when it was given, to

30:01.540 --> 30:08.540
whom it was given, in what circumstances it was given, and how it was given, all that

30:10.980 --> 30:17.980
sort of preamble he gives there, and then the actual Sutta starts, so now that explanation,

30:18.500 --> 30:25.500
as to where it was given, and he says, Ekam Samayam Bhagava, at one time, Bhagava means

30:25.500 --> 30:32.500
the enlightened one, the Buddha, Ekam Samayam Bhagava, Kurusu Viharati, Viharati was living,

30:37.620 --> 30:44.620
the word Viharati is not used for ordinary lay people in the language of India, Viharati

30:44.620 --> 30:51.620
is used for very enlightened persons, and even those who are on the path of enlightenment,

30:53.700 --> 31:00.700
like the monks, the nuns, or even lay people who are practicing Dhamma, this word is used,

31:01.460 --> 31:08.460
Viharati, so Buddha was at that time, he was living in the world of the enlightened, and

31:08.460 --> 31:15.460
in Dhamma, this word is used, Viharati, so Buddha was at that time living, staying in

31:17.940 --> 31:24.940
Kuru, Kuru was one of the sixteen states of northern India of those days, it is somewhere

31:24.940 --> 31:31.940
near today's Delhi, near Punjab, adjacent to Rajasthan, which is now called Haryana,

31:34.700 --> 31:41.700
a state which is now called Haryana, was called Kuru in those days, and it was here that this

31:42.740 --> 31:49.740
discourse was given, Ekam Samayam Bhagava, Kurusu Viharati, Viharati, Viharati, Viharati,

31:49.940 --> 31:56.940
that this discourse was given, Ekam Samayam Bhagava, Kurusu Viharati, and in Kuru, in

31:57.820 --> 32:04.820
this state also where, Kammas Dhammanam Kurunam Nigamu, a small district of this state by

32:08.140 --> 32:15.140
the name of Kammas Dhamma, this was the name of this place where this discourse was given,

32:15.140 --> 32:22.140
this discourse was given, Tattrakho Bhagava Bhikkhu Aamante Shri Bhikkha Bhooti, Buddha

32:28.180 --> 32:35.180
called those who were present, called them as O Bhikkhus, and Bhadan Te Bhikkhu Bhagavato

32:35.180 --> 32:42.180
Pachasosum, and those Bhikkhus, they replied back, Bhadan Te, yes Vendables Sir.

32:49.580 --> 32:56.580
Now two things to understand, this important sermon was given in Kuru, Buddha had very

32:56.580 --> 33:03.580
high words to say about the people of Kuru, and not only Buddha, later on also, in other

33:07.940 --> 33:14.940
traditions also, Kuru is taken as a place where people, most of the people live the

33:17.540 --> 33:24.540
life of Buddha, and Kuru is taken as a place where people, most of the people live the

33:27.020 --> 33:34.020
life of Buddha, and Kuru is taken as a place where people live the life of Buddha, and

33:41.420 --> 33:48.420
Kuru is taken as a place where people live the life of Buddha, and Kuru is taken as

33:48.460 --> 33:55.460
the field of Dhamma, the field of Kuru, it talks of Kuru, which is the field of Dhamma,

33:56.540 --> 34:03.540
why it is taken with such high regard, Buddha explains in one of his other discourses, long

34:04.940 --> 34:11.940
ago, when Buddha was not Buddha, in his previous lives, he had the seed of Buddhahood, he was

34:12.300 --> 34:18.980
developing his parmes to become Buddha, the ten parmes, and from life to life, he was

34:18.980 --> 34:25.980
living a good life to develop his own parme, in one of the lives, he was king of Kuru,

34:28.620 --> 34:35.620
now the people of Kuru, right from the king, to the smallest person, they all observe Sheela,

34:36.540 --> 34:43.540
they all observe Sheela, those were the days, when what you call Pancha Sheela now, the

34:47.140 --> 34:54.140
five precepts, what you call Sheela Dhamma, the Dhamma of Sheela, morality, in the language

34:54.780 --> 35:01.780
of those days of India, it was called Kuru Dhamma, the Dhamma of Kuru, that means the

35:02.540 --> 35:08.300
people of Kuru have got this nature, this is their nature, they live the life of morality,

35:08.300 --> 35:15.300
everyone lives the life of morality, quite peculiar, at that time, the would-be Buddha,

35:18.780 --> 35:25.780
the Bodhisatta, was the ruler of this country, Kuru, and it so happened, that one of the

35:26.780 --> 35:33.780
states of India of those days, which is today called Orissa, in those days it was called

35:35.420 --> 35:42.420
Kalinga, there was famine, drought, year after year, year after year, people became very

35:45.420 --> 35:52.420
miserable, and there was a belief, that these famines come, when people don't live the life

35:53.300 --> 35:59.940
of morality, and people don't live the life of morality, when the ruler is not living

35:59.940 --> 36:06.940
the life of morality, so the elders of this state, this kingdom, went to the king, to

36:08.500 --> 36:14.980
the ruler, and said, sir, there is something wrong, look year after year, famine is there,

36:14.980 --> 36:20.580
something should be done, our people should live the life of morality, and this cannot

36:20.580 --> 36:27.180
happen unless you start living the life of morality, so take five precepts, and let all

36:27.180 --> 36:33.820
the public, all the people of the state take five precepts and observe, and to take five

36:33.820 --> 36:40.820
precepts, it is important that it is taken from somebody, who is perfect in five precepts,

36:44.260 --> 36:50.180
so from whom you should take five precepts, from whom we should take five precepts, we

36:50.180 --> 36:56.980
better approach the ruler of Kuru, he is a perfect person, and all his people, all his

36:56.980 --> 37:03.300
subjects, they are living the life of morality, the five precepts are there, so two ambassadors

37:03.300 --> 37:10.300
were sent to the kingdom of Kuru, two Brahmin ambassadors, they reached there, and told

37:13.180 --> 37:19.620
the whole story to the ruler, we are in difficulty, please give us these five precepts, you write

37:19.620 --> 37:25.580
it on a slate, and we will take that, and on your behalf, we will read out to the teacher,

37:25.580 --> 37:30.100
and then we will read out to all the people, and we will start practicing, and we will

37:30.100 --> 37:37.100
be out of misery, the king refuses, he says, yes I have been living a perfect life of Seela,

37:40.260 --> 37:47.260
but there is one slight mistake which I committed, one slight mistake, so I am not perfect,

37:49.860 --> 37:56.860
and he asked his ambassadors, you better go to him, he asked them to go to his mother,

37:57.300 --> 38:03.980
elderly mother, she is perfect, they go to the mother, mother says no, no, no, this one

38:03.980 --> 38:10.980
little mistake I did in my life, you better go to the queen, the chief queen, and they

38:11.220 --> 38:17.680
go to the chief queen, and she says no, no, no, no, one little mistake I have done, then

38:17.720 --> 38:23.240
go to the younger brother of the king, and then go to the prime minister of the state,

38:23.240 --> 38:29.400
then go to this revenue minister of the state, then you go to the chief priest of the state,

38:29.400 --> 38:34.360
then you go to this chief officer of the state, revenue officer of the state, then you go

38:34.360 --> 38:41.360
to this chief trader of the state, business man of the state, and like this they went

38:41.360 --> 38:47.680
And like this they went on going to different, different, everyone says it was slight, slight

38:47.680 --> 38:53.080
mistake in my life, slight mistake in my life.

38:53.080 --> 38:59.280
And coming down, down, down, the charioteer, go to the charioteer.

38:59.280 --> 39:03.360
They went to the charioteer, he says no, some mistake.

39:03.360 --> 39:09.000
Then go to the watchman who takes care of the gate.

39:09.000 --> 39:10.000
Some mistake.

39:10.000 --> 39:19.360
Like this from the king down, everybody are so very much careful about their precepts.

39:19.360 --> 39:24.640
And the mistakes that they have said, we won't go in all those details, it will take time,

39:24.640 --> 39:26.600
are so flimsy.

39:26.600 --> 39:31.600
Like for example, the king he says, I made a mistake, what mistake?

39:31.600 --> 39:38.960
He says once I was showing my art of archery, I am wonderful in using the bow and the arrow

39:39.920 --> 39:45.920
and I was just showing this to my people, my subject.

39:45.920 --> 39:52.080
And one arrow which I threw, it went and fall in the pond nearby.

39:52.080 --> 39:57.760
And when it fell in the pond, it went inside and didn't come up.

39:57.760 --> 39:59.720
It didn't come up.

39:59.720 --> 40:05.600
That shows it must have pierced some fish there and with the weight of the dead fish

40:05.600 --> 40:07.520
it remained, it didn't come up.

40:08.080 --> 40:13.960
Well, who knows, whether really it pierced a fish or it might have gone in the depth

40:13.960 --> 40:18.600
of the mud at the bottom and would not have come up or some other obstacle.

40:18.600 --> 40:28.960
But he doubts, perhaps, perhaps by my action, one fish would have been killed, unlike that.

40:28.960 --> 40:32.880
People are so careful about their shield.

40:32.880 --> 40:41.520
Now this is a country where from the past tradition people are careful about their morality.

40:41.520 --> 40:47.160
So this discourse does not talk about morality, morality base is there, he is talking to the

40:47.160 --> 40:51.720
people of that country.

40:51.720 --> 40:59.800
Base of morality is essential, but base is base.

40:59.800 --> 41:08.040
The gap between one Buddha and the another Buddha, this is what happens.

41:08.040 --> 41:13.520
When a Buddha arises, an enlightened person arises, he gives complete dhamma, the totality

41:13.520 --> 41:21.800
of it, pure dhamma, there is nothing which can be taken out of it, there is no trace

41:21.800 --> 41:27.920
of impurity that has to be taken out, there is nothing wanting which has to be added,

41:28.040 --> 41:35.160
keval paripunam, keval parishuddham, the dhamma that is taught by an enlightened person is

41:35.160 --> 41:38.640
so complete and so pure.

41:38.640 --> 41:47.360
But as time passes, as time passes, this complete pure dhamma becomes incomplete, incomplete.

41:47.360 --> 41:55.880
Certain important portions get disappearing, they disappear, they disappear.

41:56.840 --> 42:04.560
The most difficult ones, they start disappearing earlier, the panya starts disappearing, vipashana

42:04.560 --> 42:07.320
starts disappearing.

42:07.320 --> 42:13.880
The panya which remains is panya, only intellectual panya, people keep on talking about panya,

42:13.880 --> 42:19.920
keep on talking about wisdom, but the practice, the bhavana maya panya gets lost.

42:19.960 --> 42:30.240
The samadhi, the purer part of samadhi goes away, the concentration, concentration with

42:30.240 --> 42:35.480
some verbalisation or visualisation or imagination, that will remain.

42:35.480 --> 42:44.040
But the samadhi which develops with the awareness of the reality, that passes away.

42:44.160 --> 42:47.160
And what remains is sila.

42:47.160 --> 42:53.840
And now that sila becomes so important to people, yes, it is important, but the other

42:53.840 --> 43:02.040
factors, the other steps of dhamma are lost, then more importance is given to sila.

43:02.040 --> 43:09.360
People start going to extreme, they start stretching the sila, one sila or the other

43:09.880 --> 43:13.520
to such an extent that the mind becomes unbalanced.

43:13.520 --> 43:18.440
They can't practice proper samadhi, they can't practice proper panya.

43:18.440 --> 43:23.880
We find same thing happening in today's India also, there are sections of the society where

43:23.880 --> 43:31.760
they stretch one sila or the other to such an extent, to such an extent that they lose

43:31.760 --> 43:33.160
the balance of their mind.

43:33.160 --> 43:38.040
They can't practice proper samadhi, they can't practice proper panya.

43:38.040 --> 43:42.880
This is what Buddha kept on condemning.

43:42.880 --> 43:53.120
He said, sila vata paramasya, paramasya is attachment, attachment to such a great extent

43:53.120 --> 43:59.880
that by observing this particular sila, I am going to get liberation, I will be liberated

43:59.880 --> 44:03.880
just by observing this one particular sila.

44:03.880 --> 44:08.000
And that makes the people so unbalanced, they don't practice samadhi, they don't practice

44:08.000 --> 44:13.080
vipashna, they don't practice panya, and they get stuck only with sila because they have

44:13.080 --> 44:14.560
stretched it so much.

44:14.560 --> 44:21.800
Vata, you take a vow, and you become so attached to this vow, and again you stretch it, stretch

44:21.800 --> 44:27.480
it, stretch it to such an extreme, nothing wrong in sila, it's so important.

44:27.480 --> 44:33.240
Nothing wrong in vata, taking vow, it is so important, like you take a vow, after midday

44:33.400 --> 44:38.560
you won't take any meals, it's a good vow, it helps you in your meditation, or at times

44:38.560 --> 44:44.960
you take a vow, you will fast for the whole day, nothing wrong, it keeps you healthy.

44:44.960 --> 44:52.000
But then people start stretching it to such an extent, you fasted for one day, I will

44:52.000 --> 44:57.840
fast for two days, I am a bigger dhamma person than you are, two days I will fast for five

44:57.840 --> 45:03.680
days, five days, I will fast for ten days, twenty days, one month, stretching, stretching,

45:03.680 --> 45:10.160
the essence gets lost, the purpose gets lost, one gets so much attached to this sila and

45:10.160 --> 45:16.880
to this vata that the other important parts of dhamma like samadhi, like panya is lost

45:16.880 --> 45:18.080
to the country.

45:18.080 --> 45:25.960
And this was the situation of kuru at that time, people are good in sila, well it is

45:25.960 --> 45:32.020
wrong to stretch it to that extent, but still those people who observe sila are definitely

45:32.020 --> 45:37.720
much much better than those who know sila, their life is without sila, so these people

45:37.720 --> 45:39.080
are much better.

45:39.080 --> 45:45.680
Now these people will understand dhamma better because their base is good, although something

45:45.680 --> 45:52.580
is wanting and that wanting can be fulfilled by this technique which is being taught now.

45:52.580 --> 45:58.780
So this is the place kuru, where the base of morality is there and this is the place

45:58.780 --> 46:03.860
where people will understand the details of this technique much better and he gives his

46:03.860 --> 46:06.300
technique there.

46:06.300 --> 46:15.140
And then when he says, oh bhikkhus come, bhikkhu, what bhikkhu?

46:15.140 --> 46:21.100
In the ordinary language of India bhikkhu means a monk, a recluse, but here it doesn't

46:21.100 --> 46:23.140
mean that.

46:23.140 --> 46:31.060
Not only here in all his teachings when he says bhikkhu, one who is practicing the teaching

46:31.060 --> 46:39.460
of dhamma, he may be a layman, he may be a householder, anyone makes no difference,

46:39.460 --> 46:47.260
a man, a woman, a monk, a nun, a householder, man, woman, anyone from all these four groups

46:47.260 --> 46:48.800
can be a bhikkhu.

46:48.800 --> 46:56.680
So he talks, when he calls bhikkhu, he calls bhikkhu to a meditator, oh meditators.

46:56.680 --> 47:01.000
And then he says, now here it starts, his discourse.

47:01.000 --> 47:18.500
Ekayanu ayam bhikkave maggu, ekayanu, one and only path, ekayanu maggu ayam bhikkave,

47:18.500 --> 47:28.880
path maggu, sattanam visuddhiya, to purify the individuals.

47:28.880 --> 47:36.080
That means to purify the mind of the individual, mental purification is the real purification,

47:36.080 --> 47:40.760
one may keep on washing one's body at the external level, this is not the purification

47:40.760 --> 47:47.280
of the individual, the mind should get purified, sattanam visuddhiya.

47:47.280 --> 47:59.980
Then what this purification does, soka paridevanam samatikamaya, soka.

47:59.980 --> 48:11.300
Great grief, mental grief, very deep grief is soka.

48:11.300 --> 48:19.660
Soka paridevanam, and with this mental grief inside, it manifests itself at the physical

48:19.660 --> 48:32.460
level, one starts crying, weeping, lamenting, samatikamaya, this path will help the meditator

48:32.460 --> 48:37.960
to transcend this, to cross this over.

48:37.960 --> 48:45.600
As you practice this technique, no more crying, no more weeping, no more lamentation, and

48:45.600 --> 48:54.220
such deep griefs, they come on the surface and pass away, you pass over them.

48:54.220 --> 49:07.960
And then, dukkha domanasanam atthangamaya, dukkha domanas, again domanas is the unpleasant

49:07.960 --> 49:15.580
feeling of the mind, mind feels unhappy, is domanas.

49:15.580 --> 49:23.480
And dukkha, the sensations on the body, unpleasant sensations on the body is dukkha, unpleasant

49:23.500 --> 49:32.500
feeling of the mind is domanas atthangamaya, to eradicate that, to finish that, this technique

49:32.500 --> 49:34.260
will help.

49:34.260 --> 49:42.340
You start from the very gross reality, very gross miseries, and you come to the subtler

49:42.340 --> 49:48.300
miseries, subtler miseries, subtler miseries, till you eradicate total miseries, no more

49:48.300 --> 49:50.540
misery.

49:50.560 --> 49:56.880
When you are too much in mental grief, then you cry and weep, this is so gross, both of

49:56.880 --> 49:59.000
them are so gross.

49:59.000 --> 50:04.760
Then the misery of mind is still there, some unpleasantness is there in the mind, domanasanam,

50:04.760 --> 50:13.560
and there is sensation on the body which is unpleasant, that also goes away by this technique.

50:13.560 --> 50:29.060
Nyayas adhigamaya, to help one to walk on the path of truth, nyayas.

50:29.060 --> 50:36.780
If you don't walk on the path of truth, if you work with imagination, then the previous

50:36.780 --> 50:41.060
thing, whatever I said, cannot be attained.

50:41.060 --> 50:47.020
Your misery from the deepest level cannot be taken out, if you just work with some kind

50:47.020 --> 50:55.860
of contemplation, some kind of imagination, then your surface of the mind is working to

50:55.860 --> 51:01.820
purify itself, surface of the mind gets purified, no doubt by that, but the deepest level of

51:01.820 --> 51:07.260
the mind, where you have these deep rooted complexes, they can't come out.

51:07.260 --> 51:12.380
They will come out only when you start observing the reality as it is pertaining to mind and

51:12.380 --> 51:17.260
matter and the interconnection between the two, and you keep on observing, observing,

51:17.260 --> 51:23.380
observing, observing, from the gross apparent truth to deeper, deeper, deeper, till you

51:23.380 --> 51:30.860
reach the ultimate truth, the subtlest ultimate truth pertaining to the matter, subtlest ultimate

51:30.860 --> 51:36.860
truth pertaining to the mind, pertaining to the mental contents, and thus you are working

51:36.860 --> 51:43.100
with the truth, truth that you experience, not the truth experienced by a Buddha.

51:43.100 --> 51:47.900
The truth experienced by Buddha can liberate only one person and that person was Buddha

51:47.900 --> 51:49.780
only who was liberated.

51:49.780 --> 51:55.580
He can only show the path, every, each individual has to walk over the path step by step and

51:55.580 --> 52:03.100
must experience the truth oneself directly, directly from the grossest reality to the

52:03.100 --> 52:06.540
subtlest, subtlest, subtlest reality.

52:06.540 --> 52:14.620
So that is called nyayas adhigamaya, gamaya, you walk on it, adhigamaya, high road, you

52:14.620 --> 52:24.980
are walking on the high road of liberation, nibbanas sacchikiriaya, and where it takes

52:24.980 --> 52:32.380
your observation of the truth from the grossest apparent reality moving towards subtlest,

52:32.380 --> 52:39.180
subtlest, but truth, no imagination, subtlest, subtlest, subtlest, subtlest reality pertaining

52:39.180 --> 52:47.660
to the entire mind matter field and then you transcend and witness something which is beyond

52:47.660 --> 52:51.740
mind and matter and which is called nibbana.

52:51.740 --> 52:57.580
The entire field of mind and matter is the field where things keep on arising, passing,

52:58.300 --> 53:04.780
arising, passing, arising, passing, sometimes arising at a very gross level, it arises seem

53:04.780 --> 53:10.220
to stay for some time and then passes away, it arises seem to stay for some time and passes

53:10.220 --> 53:16.180
away, as you go deeper, deeper, deeper, you notice that it arises, passes, arises, passes

53:16.180 --> 53:22.380
with great rapidity, even at the subtlest level there is some oscillation going on,

53:22.380 --> 53:28.380
arising, passing, arising, passing is going on, so entire field of mind and matter is

53:28.380 --> 53:34.180
the field of arising, passing, arising, passing, this is what one has to experience, not just

53:34.180 --> 53:39.500
accept it at the intellectual level, one has to experience it, then a stage comes where

53:39.500 --> 53:45.580
you transcend this field of mind and matter, you transcend this field of anicca, arising,

53:45.580 --> 53:51.820
passing, arising, passing, and something is experienced, the ultimate truth which is beyond

53:51.820 --> 53:59.900
mind and matter, where nothing arises, nothing passes away, but no words can explain it,

54:01.260 --> 54:07.980
because this is the experience where all your sense organs stop working.

54:10.780 --> 54:17.020
When somebody is in that stage of nibbana, while practicing vipashyana, one comes to the stage

54:17.020 --> 54:23.100
where one has transcended the entire field of mind and matter and is now experiencing nibbana,

54:24.460 --> 54:30.380
this experience of nibbana is beyond mind and matter, beyond the entire sensorium,

54:31.100 --> 54:38.620
all the six sense organs stop working, eyes, ears, nose, tongue, body, and mind, they stop working,

54:39.260 --> 54:46.460
this is the experience beyond the sensual field, sensory field, and coming back from that,

54:46.460 --> 54:50.780
this experience may be for a few moments, this experience can be for a few seconds,

54:50.780 --> 54:55.260
can be for a few minutes, can be for a few hours, it depends, but when you come back again,

54:56.220 --> 55:00.620
in this field, the sensorium field, the field of mind and matter, you are a changed person

55:00.620 --> 55:07.420
altogether, but you can't explain what you experienced, how will you explain, you don't

55:07.420 --> 55:14.460
have the tools to explain, that experience was experienced beyond the sense organs, and it cannot

55:14.460 --> 55:20.060
be explained by these sense organs, and it cannot be understood by the people with the sense organs,

55:20.060 --> 55:31.500
it has to be experienced by each individual, the entire path is a path of experience, experience,

55:31.500 --> 55:37.740
if you play the game of intellect, then of course you can discuss it, you give a big description of

55:37.740 --> 55:43.580
it, because you understood the intellect level, and you try to explain again at the intellect level,

55:43.580 --> 55:50.700
and people also try to understand at the intellect level, that doesn't work, the entire path must be

55:50.700 --> 55:56.300
experience, experience, that is why the dhamma, the six qualities of dhamma that he gave,

55:56.860 --> 56:05.740
the last and the most important quality of dhamma, the dhamma must be experienced

56:06.540 --> 56:11.580
by each individual within oneself, directly by oneself,

56:14.620 --> 56:18.860
you have to experience it yourself, vedana is experiencing,

56:20.780 --> 56:27.020
you experience the truth within yourself, and as you start observing and feeling and

56:27.020 --> 56:33.260
experiencing the truth within yourself, from the process, you keep on moving, moving, moving,

56:33.260 --> 56:38.700
you explore the entire field of mind and matter, and then you experience something which is beyond

56:38.700 --> 56:45.580
mind and matter, so the entire field of observing the truth personally, at the experiential level,

56:47.020 --> 56:59.340
now when he says, to people who have not walked on this path deeply, or who have not walked at all,

56:59.340 --> 57:08.140
outsiders, they will feel uncomfortable, what this person says, this is the only path,

57:09.180 --> 57:15.740
this is very narrow minded outlook, there can be so many paths, why only this path, why he says this

57:15.740 --> 57:23.100
is the only path, but those who walk over the path, it becomes so clear, what is path after all,

57:24.060 --> 57:30.620
law of nature is universal, law of nature is not different for followers of Budhha, law of nature is not

57:30.620 --> 57:35.340
different for those who call themselves Hindus, or those who call themselves Christian, or those who

57:35.340 --> 57:41.420
call themselves Muslims, law of nature is law of nature, and he wants us to experience the law of

57:41.420 --> 57:47.980
nature, to understand the law of nature, the truth, the law which is applicable to one and all,

57:48.620 --> 57:53.020
the dhamma which is applicable to one and all, the nature the characteristic,

57:53.020 --> 57:57.460
Like the characteristic of fire is to burn.

57:57.460 --> 58:03.140
Anyone who places his hand on the fire is bound to get burned.

58:03.140 --> 58:05.260
The fire will not discriminate.

58:05.260 --> 58:09.060
Fire will not see that the hand is of the hand of a Hindu or a Buddhist or a Christian

58:09.060 --> 58:12.540
or a Australian or a New Zealander or an American.

58:12.540 --> 58:15.480
Anyone who puts the hand on the fire is bound to get burned.

58:15.480 --> 58:17.880
I don't like burning my hand.

58:17.880 --> 58:20.340
So I better keep my hand away from the fire.

58:20.340 --> 58:22.100
This is law of nature.

58:22.100 --> 58:23.580
This is dhamma.

58:23.580 --> 58:25.660
This is what it teaches.

58:25.660 --> 58:28.080
This is universal.

58:28.080 --> 58:32.580
Because the law is universal, therefore the path has to be universal.

58:32.580 --> 58:34.300
It can't be sectarian.

58:34.300 --> 58:37.180
And universal path can be only one.

58:37.180 --> 58:39.140
Because the law is only one.

58:39.140 --> 58:42.980
Buddha or no Buddha, the law is law.

58:42.980 --> 58:45.220
It remains.

58:45.220 --> 58:49.340
Even when somebody does not become Buddha, the law of nature is there.

58:49.340 --> 58:50.840
It remains.

58:50.840 --> 58:54.600
Even when somebody becomes a Buddha, the law of nature is there.

58:54.600 --> 59:01.200
And even after Buddha, the law of nature is there.

59:01.200 --> 59:06.880
Like someone by the name of Newton discovered this law of gravity.

59:06.880 --> 59:11.180
Newton or no Newton, this law of gravity was there even before Newton.

59:11.180 --> 59:15.480
Even at the time of Newton, even after Newton, it was good that somebody discovered it and

59:15.480 --> 59:16.480
placed before it.

59:16.480 --> 59:18.680
We make use of it.

59:18.680 --> 59:23.800
The law of relativity, somebody by the name of Einstein found it out.

59:23.800 --> 59:24.800
It was there.

59:24.800 --> 59:28.720
Whether Einstein or no Einstein, even before Einstein, the law of relativity was there

59:28.720 --> 59:34.860
at the time of Einstein, and even after Einstein, similarly, dhamma is there.

59:34.860 --> 59:40.280
If this, this is there, this result is bound to come, law of nature.

59:40.280 --> 59:48.080
If you do not want this result to come, then this, this should be avoided, law of nature.

59:48.080 --> 59:52.680
You keep this and this, and you don't want the result, not possible.

59:52.680 --> 59:58.240
A kaino maggo in the sense that you follow the law of nature, and law of nature is one

59:58.240 --> 01:00:00.600
and only one.

01:00:00.600 --> 01:00:05.640
Two parts of hydrogen, one part of oxygen.

01:00:05.640 --> 01:00:09.680
This results in moisture, in water, law of nature.

01:00:09.680 --> 01:00:12.080
This is law, this is dhamma.

01:00:12.080 --> 01:00:17.440
If there is no oxygen, in a planet there is no oxygen, or no hydrogen, there is no water,

01:00:17.440 --> 01:00:20.480
no moisture, law of nature.

01:00:20.480 --> 01:00:25.480
This is what you will understand the whole path as you proceed, you have worked already,

01:00:25.480 --> 01:00:31.960
and you will work much deeper, that if this, this happens, this result is bound to come.

01:00:31.960 --> 01:00:36.760
And if you don't want this result, because the result is not pleasant to you, it's misery,

01:00:36.760 --> 01:00:41.520
and you want to come out of misery, then this, this should not happen, you have to remove,

01:00:41.520 --> 01:00:46.360
you have to remove the cause, and the result is automatically removed.

01:00:46.440 --> 01:00:52.000
Without removing the cause, somebody feels that I will get liberated from the fruit of

01:00:52.000 --> 01:01:00.000
this cause, the unpleasant fruit of this cause, the bitter fruit of this cause, because somebody,

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:05.520
some supernatural power will be very kind to me, that in spite of all the impurities

01:01:05.520 --> 01:01:09.040
in my mind, this person will liberate me.

01:01:09.040 --> 01:01:13.280
Well, this is just wishful thinking, it does not happen.

01:01:13.320 --> 01:01:21.120
Everyone has to work, and this is the way, the law, the nature, that you have to eradicate

01:01:21.120 --> 01:01:27.000
your impurities, you have to eradicate your present habit, pattern, full of ignorance,

01:01:27.000 --> 01:01:31.960
where you keep on generating sankaras, and as a result of which you keep on suffering

01:01:31.960 --> 01:01:33.360
from misery.

01:01:33.360 --> 01:01:39.680
This pattern of your habit, at a very deep level of the mind, has to be changed, and

01:01:39.680 --> 01:01:41.360
this is what is being done.

01:01:41.360 --> 01:01:46.240
That is why Ekayanu Maggu, Ekayanu Maggu.

01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:49.360
And what is this Ekayanu Maggu?

01:01:49.360 --> 01:02:03.640
He says Yadidam, and this is Chattaro Satipatthana, the four types of Satipatthana, establishment

01:02:03.640 --> 01:02:10.320
of awareness with wisdom in four ways.

01:02:10.320 --> 01:02:13.480
And what are these four ways?

01:02:13.480 --> 01:02:17.360
Katame Chattaro, what are these four ways?

01:02:17.360 --> 01:02:22.640
Idhavikkave Bhikkhu, oh Bhikkhus, oh meditators.

01:02:22.640 --> 01:02:24.640
Here a meditator, what he does?

01:02:24.640 --> 01:02:39.200
Kaaye Kayanupassi Viharati, Aatapi Sampajanau Satima, Vinaya Loke Abhijya Dho Manasang.

01:02:39.200 --> 01:02:50.600
One witnesses the reality of the body within the body, Kaaye Kayanupassi, Aatapi, very

01:02:50.600 --> 01:02:59.320
ardently, diligently, Sampajanau with wisdom, the wisdom of arising, passing, arising, passing,

01:02:59.320 --> 01:03:02.160
Satima with awareness.

01:03:02.160 --> 01:03:11.960
One is fully aware, with wisdom, the truth pertaining to the body by observing the truth

01:03:11.960 --> 01:03:15.320
within the body itself, that means no imagination.

01:03:15.320 --> 01:03:21.900
You are directly experiencing the truth about your body within your body.

01:03:21.900 --> 01:03:29.840
And so also, Vedanasu Vedananupassi Viharati, you are observing the truth of these body

01:03:29.920 --> 01:03:34.560
sensations within body sensations, you are not imagining them, you are experiencing them,

01:03:34.560 --> 01:03:38.160
you have a direct experience of that.

01:03:38.160 --> 01:03:47.960
Vedanasu Vedananupassi Viharati, Aatapi Sampajanau Satima, very diligently, with awareness, with

01:03:47.960 --> 01:03:48.960
wisdom.

01:03:48.960 --> 01:03:56.760
Vinaya Loke Abhijya Dho Manasang, keeping oneself away from craving and aversion, craving

01:03:56.760 --> 01:04:02.880
and aversion towards the phenomena, the mind-matter phenomena, which is called Loke.

01:04:02.880 --> 01:04:10.920
Chitte Chittanupassi Viharati, similarly observing the reality of mind within the mind.

01:04:10.920 --> 01:04:18.920
And Dhammesu Dhammanupassi Viharati, the mental contents, the law of nature, the reality pertaining

01:04:18.920 --> 01:04:26.040
to the law of mind and matter, within this law, within the mental contents, you observe

01:04:26.040 --> 01:04:34.040
the mental contents, within the mental contents, again, Aatapi Sampajanau Satima, with full

01:04:34.040 --> 01:04:41.240
awareness, full wisdom and working diligently, Vinaya Loke Abhijya Dho Manasang, keeping

01:04:41.240 --> 01:04:44.600
yourself free from craving, free from aversion.

01:04:44.600 --> 01:04:48.500
We'll go in detail of this paragraph tomorrow.

01:04:48.500 --> 01:04:57.340
In the meantime, understand that all the four Satipatthanas, observing the truth pertaining

01:04:57.340 --> 01:05:04.660
to the body, observing the truth pertaining to the sensations on the body, observing

01:05:04.660 --> 01:05:10.140
the truth pertaining to the mind, observing the truth pertaining to the contents of the

01:05:10.140 --> 01:05:21.600
mind, all these four must be experienced by each meditator directly, himself or herself.

01:05:21.600 --> 01:05:27.280
Just intellectualizing it does not help you.

01:05:27.280 --> 01:05:32.060
To understand Dhamma intellectually is good because it will give you inspiration, because

01:05:32.060 --> 01:05:36.700
it will give you guidance, it will make you understand how you should practice, how you

01:05:36.700 --> 01:05:41.420
should experience, but actually it is your own experience which is going to give result

01:05:41.420 --> 01:05:44.820
and this you will understand as you proceed further.

01:05:44.820 --> 01:05:50.060
In the meantime, now you are working with your respiration, the reality of this moment,

01:05:50.060 --> 01:05:58.500
be aware of it, work with it, coming, going as it is, as it is, deep, shallow, as it is,

01:05:58.500 --> 01:06:03.900
touching here, touching there, as it is, the sensation below the nostrils, as it is, from

01:06:03.980 --> 01:06:11.060
moment to moment, moment to moment, try to maintain this continuity of the awareness

01:06:11.060 --> 01:06:17.980
of the reality, this is your object now, this area of the body, you are working on the body,

01:06:17.980 --> 01:06:22.700
this area of the body, the reality that is manifested from moment to moment, from moment

01:06:22.700 --> 01:06:29.140
to moment, you are aware, you are aware, day and night you are aware, accept the period

01:06:29.140 --> 01:06:35.320
when you are in deep sleep. Most of the time you will forget. And your mind will start

01:06:35.320 --> 01:06:39.320
wandering here and there. You can't help. But as soon as you realize the mind has wandered

01:06:39.320 --> 01:06:44.640
away, well, bring back. Just accept the fact, mind has wandered away. Don't generate a feeling

01:06:44.640 --> 01:06:49.700
of disappointment or depression when you find the mind has wandered away. Just accept, mind

01:06:49.700 --> 01:06:54.320
has wandered away. Now again, let me start. Start again with the breath coming in, going

01:06:54.320 --> 01:06:59.640
out, coming in, going out, deep, shallow, whatever it is, and the sensation on this

01:06:59.640 --> 01:07:03.920
area. You are aware of this area. You are aware of the breath coming in, going out,

01:07:03.920 --> 01:07:08.720
coming in, going out. And proceed. You have been working on this. Now you will work more

01:07:08.720 --> 01:07:15.200
seriously, more diligently. Time is very short. And you have come to a very serious course

01:07:15.200 --> 01:07:20.640
with all the atmosphere around you. So serious. Everybody is working so seriously. No disturbance

01:07:20.640 --> 01:07:25.760
for the new students. Make use of it. Make use of it, not obliging anybody else, for

01:07:25.760 --> 01:07:32.760
your own good, for your own benefit, for your own liberation. To enjoy real peace, real

01:07:34.760 --> 01:07:41.760
harmony, real happiness. May all of you enjoy real peace, real harmony, real happiness.

01:08:20.640 --> 01:08:28.240
May all of you enjoy real peace, real harmony, real happiness.

01:08:50.640 --> 01:08:57.640
Take rest for a few minutes, and take rest with awareness, with awareness, and then come

01:09:01.120 --> 01:09:08.120
back and start working with awareness, with awareness.

